  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners: South Africa &#x2013; Start Up Challenge</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There are four targets for this project:1.	To create and externally communicate five concrete showcases embodied in a business or startup challenge, in which five South African (SA) startups (around two to three years old) and five Dutch disruptive thinkers with entrepreneurial experience work together as teams to develop solutions for a problem experienced and articulated by the participating startups.2.	The project is directly related to the MIB of the SA Missions, in which entrepreneurship is one of the main focuses. The Netherlands embassy is busy rolling out Orange Corners, a take-off platform for SA entrepreneurs and simultaneously a landing platform for Dutch entrepreneurs in existing structures of Maboneng &amp; Diepsloot, and possibly Johannesburg, Durban and Cape Town. That is an opportunity for the Dutch and South African startups that partake in the challenge to connect with the Orange Corners for the teams to have several touch points with the two linked events (Innovation Summit and Open Design Cape Town 2016) to generate exposure for their challenge and businesses and develop the participant&#x2019;s knowledge and networks.3.	During their stay, the teams aim to make significant progress in their challenge while developing hard and soft skills. 4.	They will also gain an understanding of the local challenges in Africa and establish stronger connections between the innovation sectors in the Netherlands and South Africa, setting the stage for future cooperation.</narrative>
  </description>
